{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1792883931,"nonce":"wM9Q/hurLwCe/1eG1FXE9NxORoI=","message":"Implemented editor groups as a binary layout of resizable rows and columns. Each group has its own tab strip, active page and focus indicator. Toolbar buttons beside the actions menu split right or down; the menu also moves the editor to another group, joins all groups and closes a group without dropping its tabs. Commands are available through the command center and desktop View menus.\n\nSplitting moves the current tab when other tabs remain; a single-tab group opens an empty pane. A tab keeps one owner, preserving its document/undo state and extension-mounted root. Already-open files focus their owning group. Code, extension previews and images remain mounted while visible in another group. Workspace sessions retain the nested layout, divider proportions, group tab order and selections while accepting older flat sessions and pruning missing files.\n\nDefault shortcuts: Mod+backslash splits right, Mod+Alt+backslash splits down, Mod+Alt+Right/Left focuses groups. Mod is Command on macOS and Control elsewhere. The former macOS terminal shortcut moves to Ctrl+Shift+5 to avoid a conflict. Settings can override all bindings. Editor group shortcuts are handled before caret navigation and reserved while a terminal has focus.\n\nFocus is transferred after queued pane replacements. Completion/code-action ownership follows the focused editor; disposal clears the mounted-editor reference. Empty synchronization checks for changed values before writing native string signals, preventing a self-invalidating Close All loop. A focused core regression checks stabilization while idle. Temporary dependency tracing was restored and is not part of the change.\n\nValidation passed:\n- Full Checks suite, including editor-group ownership, nested splits, moving/joining/closure, renames, missing-file pruning, empty-pane focus, session round trips, idle synchronization and shortcut conflicts for macOS/other platforms.\n- Split UI fixture in both themes: both directions, actual pointer/menu/keyboard focus, stable visible editors, Find routing, undo/redo, keyboard divider resizing, SVG and extension previews, restoration/unsaved recovery, repeated joins/splits and final document release. Captures inspected in both schemes.\n- Existing WorkspaceSessionLifecycle, documents, find and views UI regressions.\n- Desktop rayde.Main build with ashui_window.\n- 17 local documentation links resolve; diff passes whitespace checks.\n\nUser instructions are in docs/editor.md and docs/keys.md; contributor architecture and checks remain in docs/contributing.\n\nLanded locally as c056d6d9d5b3fe2cfca2b52e2913d83bc2587b03 (Add resizable editor groups and split shortcuts).","files":null}]}